title The room that said what it is

prompt The fleet baton, seat petrichor: the docs-geode shelf and the prose product, grade what you touch and raise what reads below B.

rota lap 4249, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in: the concrete fact taken in at the door before anyone argues with it. Threshold plus the fixed seat, context/TWO_ROOMS.md, whose whole discipline is one line read off a status line. Read against my own lane it produced a measurement rather than an opinion: of 37 living docs-geode pages, one names its room, and the doorway guard reads external-research/, active-designing/ and docs/, so it can see none of the other 36.

think My own last two logs named the same unclaimed door twice: docs-geode/etc/README.md at D+ 69. That is the thread, so I took it rather than opening something new.
think Graded it before touching it. Register 29 on 71 percent of 7 sentences, and the detail line said no single sentence could have carried it across the 20 percent ceiling. So the fault was the page's framing rather than one bad clause.
think It also sat under the 8-sentence floor, which means prose_register_scan counted it as unreadable rather than as passing. A room's own front door standing outside the meter aimed at that room is worth more than the grade alone.
think Every claim on the page is about something being absent, so the question was whether affirmative framing could hold them. It could, one at a time: belongs on none of its shelves became fits outside all of its shelves; the eleven genres became eleven rooms standing beside this one, which I checked with ls docs-geode/ rather than trusting the elder sentence.
think The second move was structural. Reach holds bold-led paragraphs out of its word count, so the closing beat was doing no work for the reading while sitting inside a bold answer it was not part of. Split out, it is a better sentence and Reach went 50 to 80.
think I gave the page its room token while I had it open, and stopped there. Widening the doorway guard to docs-geode would red eight ships for 36 pages nobody has swept, which is the price Incense measured and declined a day ago.

obs D+ 69 to B+ 89, shadow A. Register 29 to 100. Truth held at 100 on three resolving paths. The page grew from 7 to 11 sentences and every one of the four new ones carries a claim the elder page already made.
obs Tree-wide the page crossed the floor and passed: front_doors_readable 81 to 82, front_doors_unrostered_over held at 27, teaching_over_field_target unchanged at 4 of 5.
obs I made a real error and it is worth writing down plainly. I reached for tools/f/fleet_call.sh --pattern to answer a read question and omitted --dry-run. It is a caller and signals TERM by default. Every peer tree was refused by name -- the tool did exactly its job -- and my own wrapper shells took the signal, so the cold pass lost its verdict at 140 green and 0 red.
obs Worse, and earlier: the wait loops I wrote before it ran pgrep -f standing_equipment_run, whose pattern appears in the loop's own command line, so each waiter matched itself and waited forever. Twenty-five minutes went to that. Both faults are %541's shape arriving from a session rather than from a tracked file, which is exactly why that clause moved onto the baton today.
obs I chose to spend one hot pass rather than a second cold one. The tree opened clean on real evidence -- 140 guards green, zero red, tree_at_open recorded -- and the pass that measures the tree the commit ships is the more valuable of the two. Said here rather than left for a reader to notice.

file docs-geode/etc/README.md every claim restated affirmatively and the closing beat split out of its bold paragraph; D+ 69 to B+ 89, and the room token added at the door
file construction/ITINERARY.md the elder PETRICHOR account shelved, this lap's seated, git nib moved to HEAD's parent; pin at 40,950 of 40,960
file construction/archive/20260908-030301_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the elder account whole, its own shelved link re-anchored one directory shallower so it resolves from the shelf

loom prose=docs-geode/etc/README.md register_before=29 register_after=100 negatives_before_pct=71 negatives_after_pct=0 reach_before=50 reach_after=80 grade_before=10 grade_after=8 composite_before=69 composite_after=89
loom register_scan=tree front_doors=119 readable_before=81 readable_after=82 unrostered_over=27 teaching_over=4 teaching_ceiling=5
loom doorway=docs-geode pages=37 naming_room=1 silent=36 guard_reach=external-research,active-designing,docs
loom roster=cold guards_green=140 guards_red=0 verdict=lost_to_own_signal

recommend keep-going -- the same two-part move is proven twice now on two teaching doors, so the next docs-geode page reading under B is ready to take it; the one door needing your word is whether the two-rooms doorway law reaches docs-geode at all, since 36 of its 37 living pages name no room and no guard can see them.

scope grade and repair the docs-geode etc front door, the one register fault of the three my card named, and measure my own room's silence on the two-rooms door token
status GREEN on the work -- the page reads B+ 89 with its shadow at A, the tree-wide register scan reads verdict=ok with readable up one and both over-counts held; HONEST GAP on the receipt -- the cold pass ran 140 guards green and 0 red and then lost its verdict to my own mis-invoked fleet_call, so the hot pass below is this lap's full receipt rather than its second one
